UID:SC-91A97B6E-D30D-457D-B26A-5755CE0E0B87
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260822
SUMMARY:S: Write to Mathew Timmons — reconnect + offer to come back on the 
 show
DESCRIPTION:*Michael drafts this one.* Beats\, in order:\n\n1. *Reconnect\,
  briefly.* ~6.5 years. Ep. 83 with Joe\, Feb 2020\, was a\n   good time — 
 say so without a paragraph of throat-clearing.\n2. *What happened since.* 
 The opera\, in the framing language — /not/\n   "a musical version of a St
 ar Trek episode." Use the outreach\n   one-liner from . Link cdbzb.com/ope
 ra/return-to-tomorrow.html.\n3. *The ask\, and it is the only ask:* would 
 they have you back on /The\n   People/ to talk about it. One question\, an
 swerable yes/no.\n\n*Do not* ask about Human Resources\, Public Fiction\, 
 or LACE in this\nnote.  Venue routing is the /second/ conversation\, after
  the\nappearance or after he replies warmly. Opening with a venue ask\ncon
 verts a friendly reconnect into a favor request and wastes the\nstrongest 
 card in the entry.\n\n*Address to Timmons only* (`anathemata@gmail.com'). 
 Ben White can be\ncc'd if the reply turns into scheduling\, but a two-host
  cold-open\ndilutes the answerable question. Joe not needed — you were the
  guest.\n\n*Consonance check before sending:* (1) reconnect\, (2) framing 
 language\nnot "musical version of"\, (3) exactly one answerable question\,
  (4) no\nvenue ask\, (5) no rights talk.
CATEGORIES:cal,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
